Third-party code included in SPARTA
===================================

This file states WHAT is third-party and WHERE it came from.
The licence texts those origins require are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, which is
the file that must ship with every binary release.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No third-party source code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SPARTA compiles no third-party source. Its fill-reducing ordering is SCALPEL,
original SPARTA work in crates/scalpel. The Rust crates SPARTA links are listed
with their licences in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES section 4.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms followed, with no code taken
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  SPRAL SSIDS (BSD-3, (c) STFC)  the supernode amalgamation merge rule in
                                 src/symbolic/supernode.rs follows the rule
                                 described for SSIDS core_analyse.f90. No SSIDS
                                 code was used. The STFC notice is reproduced
                                 as attribution hygiene.

  LAPACK (BSD-3)                 the blocked pivoting in
                                 src/kernels/ldlt_factor.metal
                                 follows the published zsytrf/zlasyf algorithm.
                                 No LAPACK code was used.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Original SPARTA work
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything else in this repository is original and carries no third-party
licence: the Metal kernels, the GPU storage plan and dispatch schedule, the
Objective-C bridge, the whole of src/symbolic/, the SCALPEL ordering in
crates/scalpel/, the Python bindings, devtools/matgen/, and the benchmark
harness.

Within src/symbolic/, these were written from the published literature and
share no code with any existing implementation:

  column_counts.rs      Gilbert, Ng & Peyton (1994). Record in COL_COUNTS.md
                        section 7, removed in a5985e4
                        (git show a5985e4^:COL_COUNTS.md).
  elimination_tree.rs   George & Liu (1981) ch. 5; Liu (1990).
  postorder.rs          standard postorder traversal.
  supernode.rs          fundamental supernodes per Liu, Ng & Peyton (1993);
                        merge rule per SSIDS, as above.

devtools/matgen/ discretises the time-harmonic curl-curl Maxwell operator on a
structured grid. Written from the physics.

NOTHING IN THIS REPOSITORY DERIVES FROM RSLAB OR FERAL. The symbolic analysis
and fill-reducing orderings that once did were replaced between 14 and
15 September 2026. The full provenance record -- what each file was written
from, how the replacements were verified, and the limitations of that record --
is THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES section 5.1.
